46
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:05,960
Um I got involved in holography uh I um let's see now.

47
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,920
So long ago it's kind of uh thrown my mind back to the dates.

48
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:12,840
Must be late eighties, uh so around eighty eighty nine.

49
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:16,200
Uh no way back before that in fact well I'm older than I thought.

50
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:24,040
Uh must be eighty four uh I attended um what uh is over here uh uh a BA in arts, a bachelor of arts.

51
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:27,640
Uh I'm afraid I don't know what the equivalent would be for you guys over stateside.

52
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:31,160
But it was a four year um degree course in graphic design.

53
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:34,600
And at that time I had quite a strong leaning towards computer graphics.

54
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:46,240
Um but towards the end of the course kind of revived my interest in holography and managed to find a few courses that were being run by external sources like uh Richmond holographic studios who are quite famous in that field.

55
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:57,520
Um and managed to train with them and and started to actually get some hands on in holographic equipment, which I'm sure also many of your listeners will be aware is pretty hard to and expensive to get hold of even now.

56
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:02,720
What were some of the uh Richmond holographics work that you got involved with?

57
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:04,320
Any particular pieces?

58
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:09,440
It was it was not their work per se, it was the fact that they were running uh courses for the general public.

59
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:19,520
Uh so it was uh it was an easy way uh to actually go in and get uh hands on equipment in uh uh you know, hands on the holographic equipment for a fair price and be taught the sort of basics.

60
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:29,600
Um and then bringing that back into my graphic design course to to sort of show them and it was very difficult because it was all new to them so they didn't really have any way to rate it.

61
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,760
Um any way to kind of appraise it.

62
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:34,080
So I actually almost flunked that course because of that.

63
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:37,760
They they kind of just didn't know w what holography was or how it could be used.

64
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:46,480
Um but I was lucky to to get through um that that graphic design course and with a uh with a pass and then was very lucky to be accepted at the Royal College of Art.

65
